<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy - Ice Bath Timer: One Tap" description="Privacy Policy for the Ice Bath Timer: One Tap iPhone and Apple Watch app.">
  <p class="eyebrow">Ice Bath Timer: One Tap</p>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="effective">Effective date: 25 November 2026</p>

  <p>Ice Bath Timer: One Tap ("the app") is designed to respect your privacy. This policy explains, in plain terms, what the app does and does not do with information.</p>

  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <p>Ice Bath Timer: One Tap does not collect any personal information. It has no account, no sign-up and no server. The app does not use advertising, analytics or tracking of any kind, and it does not connect to the internet.</p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <p>None. We do not collect your name, email address, health data or any other information, and nothing about your use of the app is sent to us or to anyone else.</p>

  <h2>Apple Health</h2>
  <p>If you allow it, the app reads your heart rate on your Apple Watch during a bath, to show it live and on the Done screen. The app does not keep its own copy of your heart rate.</p>
  <p>So that your Apple Watch measures heart rate every few seconds, the app runs a workout session during the bath. At the end of the bath the workout is ended and discarded; it is never saved as a workout.</p>
  <p>Health data read by the app is never sent to us or to anyone else. It is used only to show it to you. If you do not allow access, the timer still works and the Done screen shows "HR unavailable".</p>

  <h2>Motion</h2>
  <p>On your iPhone, the app uses the phone's motion sensors so that tilting the phone moves the water on the calendar. On your Apple Watch, it uses the motion sensors so the water on screen leans as you turn your wrist. This motion data is used only on the device at that moment and is never stored.</p>

  <h2>Information stored on your devices</h2>
  <p>The app keeps very little, and only on your own devices:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>On your Apple Watch: your two settings (bath length and get ready length).</li>
    <li>On your iPhone: the dates of the days you finished a bath (year, month and day only), used to show the calendar.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>When a bath finishes, your Apple Watch sends that date directly to your own iPhone. This information never leaves your devices, except in your own standard Apple iCloud device backup, which is controlled entirely by you and your Apple account; we have no access to it.</p>

  <h2>Deleting your data</h2>
  <p>Deleting the app from your iPhone and Apple Watch removes all of its data, unless it remains in your own iCloud device backup under your control.</p>

  <h2>Advertising, analytics, and tracking</h2>
  <p>The app contains no advertising, no analytics and no tracking technologies. We do not build a profile of you and we do not follow you across apps or websites.</p>

  <h2>Selling or sharing data</h2>
  <p>We do not sell, rent or share any personal information with advertisers or data brokers.</p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>The app does not collect personal information from anyone, including children.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, we will update the effective date above and post the revised policy at this address.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>If you have any questions about this policy, contact <a href="mailto:support@mikhailnarbekov.com">support@mikhailnarbekov.com</a>.</p>
</LegalLayout>
